From: TDVP Device Team
Subject: [PATCH] Initialize shared ONNX schemas once before registering ORT extensions

The public ONNX provider retains its lazy automatic schema registration,
which standalone model-checking consumers require. Trigger that path before
adding ORT schemas, and avoid registering standard ONNX schemas twice.
The source-specific define is supplied only for this public-provider build.

--- a/onnxruntime/core/session/environment.cc
+++ b/onnxruntime/core/session/environment.cc
@@ -214,2 +214,5 @@
     std::call_once(schemaRegistrationOnceFlag, []() {
+#if defined(TDVP_ONNX_PUBLIC_AUTO_SCHEMA_REGISTRY)
+      (void)ONNX_NAMESPACE::OpSchemaRegistry::Schema("Identity");
+#endif
       auto& domainToVersionRangeInstance = ONNX_NAMESPACE::OpSchemaRegistry::DomainToVersionRange::Instance();
@@ -247,11 +250,13 @@
+#if !defined(TDVP_ONNX_PUBLIC_AUTO_SCHEMA_REGISTRY)
       RegisterOnnxOperatorSetSchema();
 
 #ifndef DISABLE_ML_OPS
       RegisterOnnxMLOperatorSetSchema();
 #endif
 
 #if defined(ENABLE_TRAINING_OPS)
       RegisterOnnxTrainingOperatorSetSchema();
 #endif
+#endif
 
 #if defined(ENABLE_TRAINING_OPS)
